        "title": "feat(queue): persist followup queues across gateway restarts",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen the gateway process restarts, followup messages queued during an active agent turn are silently lost.\n\n## Solution\n\nPersist followup queues in shared SQLite (`followup_queue_entries`), migrate legacy JSON sidecars via doctor, rehydrate from live config, and wake restored routes on gateway startup so production idle-kick can drain them.\n\nClassify `followup-queue-restore` heartbeats as wake payloads so empty/comment-only `HEARTBEAT.md` cannot skip restored-queue system events before drain.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Followup messages queued during an active Telegram turn survive gateway restart and are delivered afterward instead of disappearing; restored-queue recovery heartbeats also bypass `HEARTBEAT.md` idle gating so valid restored sessions outside the routine heartbeat map still drain.\n- Real environment tested: Local machine `joseph-MS-7B51`, exact-head checkout `76de7ef67c44529e74cff65b3bf902504a8de507`, Telegram DM chatId `6300969793`, sessionKey `agent:main:telegram:direct:6300969793`.\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch:\n  1. Enqueue a mid-turn Telegram followup into shared SQLite (`followup_queue_entries`) with routing selectors intact.\n  2. Simulate gateway crash (wipe in-memory queues + restore-once flag).\n  3. Restore from SQLite, request `followup-queue-restore` heartbeat wake, register drain callback, and idle-kick drain.\n  4. Confirm exactly-once delivery to Telegram DM `6300969793` and that a second restart does not replay.\n- Evidence after fix (exact head `76de7ef67c44529e74cff65b3bf902504a8de507` @ 2026-07-22T04:01:18.404Z):\n  - Live Bot API proof messageId `4531` posted to Telegram DM `6300969793`.\n  - Focused exact-head tests: **30/30 passed** (`persist`, restart round-trip, sqlite store, doctor migration, gateway recovery wake).\n  - Live proof result: `ok=True` — persisted→crash→restore→wake→drain once; second restart empty (`itemsAfterSecondRestart=0`).\n  - Marker: `PR82572-FOLLOWUP-RESTART-2026-07-22T04-01-18-404Z`\n  - Native Telegram Desktop / Mantis capture still requires write/admin on `openclaw/openclaw` (actor `jewseppi` is read-only for workflow_dispatch); maintainer can re-run `@openclaw-mantis` / label trigger if visual GIFs are still required after this exact-head evidence.\n\n\n## Tests and validation\n\nCurrent head `f49e8ee76137deb718f1e09251e2fa629a611500`:\n\n```bash\npnpm check:architecture\n```\n\nResults:\n- `pnpm check:architecture`: passed\n- queue/gateway focused verification: **42/42 tests passed**\n- GitHub `Real behavior proof`: passed\n- GitHub CI including `check-additional-runtime-topology-architecture`: passed\n\nEarlier rebuilt runtime head `a94470581b3cf10c0939b1fc6442c0431cfd0473` (local, June 15-16, 2026):\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo\n./node_modules/.bin/oxlint \\\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts \\\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.scheduler.test.ts \\\n  src/auto-reply/reply/queue/drain.ts \\\n  src/infra/state-migrations.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/gateway/server-followup-queue-recovery.test.ts \\\n  src/gateway/server-runtime-services.test.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.scheduler.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.returns-default-unset.test.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/infra/followup-queue-sqlite.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/state-migrations.test.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/auto-reply/reply/queue/persist.test.ts \\\n  src/auto-reply/reply/queue.drain-restart.test.ts \\\n  src/auto-reply/reply/queue.followup-restart-roundtrip.test.ts\n```\n\nResults:\n- `tsgo:core`: passed\n- focused oxlint on the rebased repair surface: passed\n- gateway shard: **4 files, 24 tests passed**\n- heartbeat recovery shard: **2 files, 64 tests passed**\n- SQLite + migration shard: **2 files, 12 tests passed**\n- queue persist / restart / round-trip shard: **3 files, 38 tests passed**\n\n## Notes\n\n- The old dirty PR branch was preserved separately before the clean replay; the live PR branch now points at the rebuilt queue-only branch.\n- The stale proof mismatch has been reduced here by aligning the body to the actual live head `f49e8ee76137deb718f1e09251e2fa629a611500`, explicitly separating runtime-behavior evidence from later CI-only allowlist repairs, and pointing at the fresh current-head Mantis request.\n\n\n",
